WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.330
Hi! Two short sentences can become one better sentence. Today we'll learn to combine sentences.

2
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.794
Say the shared part only once: I like cats and dogs.

3
00:00:13.944 --> 00:00:16.578
Opposite ideas use but.

4
00:00:16.728 --> 00:00:19.434
Cause then result uses so.

5
00:00:19.584 --> 00:00:24.426
Result first, reason after uses because.

6
00:00:24.576 --> 00:00:28.482
Use who for people: The girl who won is my friend.

7
00:00:28.632 --> 00:00:33.546
Use which for things and animals: I lost the bag which Mum gave me.

8
00:00:33.696 --> 00:00:38.874
When combining, drop the repeated she or it, and use who or which instead.

9
00:00:39.024 --> 00:00:44.058
After combining, check: is the meaning still the same?

10
00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:48.738
Watch out! Once you use who, you can't keep she as well!

11
00:00:48.888 --> 00:00:53.442
Who replaces she, so it's: I have a friend who lives near me.

12
00:00:53.592 --> 00:00:57.690
Read it at the end to check it flows.

13
00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:08.322
Your turn! Mei sings. Mei dances. Combine them with and. Pause and think.

14
00:01:08.472 --> 00:01:14.730
Say Mei only once: Mei sings and dances. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:25.938
Another one! The cake looked nice. It tasted bad. Combine them with but. Pause and think.

16
00:01:26.088 --> 00:01:33.378
Opposite ideas: The cake looked nice but it tasted bad. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:33.528 --> 00:01:44.538
Here's another! We took umbrellas. It was raining. Combine them with because. Pause and think.

18
00:01:44.688 --> 00:01:51.642
The rain is the reason: We took umbrellas because it was raining. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:51.792 --> 00:02:02.202
Try one more! That is the boy. He helped me. Combine them with who. Pause and think.

20
00:02:02.352 --> 00:02:08.298
Drop he: That is the boy who helped me. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:08.448 --> 00:02:19.314
Try one more! I read a book. It was about space. Combine them with which. Pause and think.

22
00:02:19.464 --> 00:02:27.690
A book is a thing, so which, and drop it: I read a book which was about space. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:38.658
Try one more! I was tired. I went to bed early. Combine them with so. Pause and think.

24
00:02:38.808 --> 00:02:46.650
Being tired is the reason, going to bed is the result, so we join them with so. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:57.042
Last one! Do you want tea? Do you want milk? Combine them with or. Pause and think.

26
00:02:57.192 --> 00:03:03.810
Say the same part only once: Do you want tea or milk? Did you get it right?

27
00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:13.770
Remember: join sentences with and, but, so or because. Use who for people and which for things, drop repeated words, and keep the meaning.

28
00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:19.505
When you write, try joining two short sentences into one!

